  (route.no-pii.test.ts:62-67), asserts no fixture value in the captured
  prompt, and keeps both math sentences (lines 121-122). Passed in my run.
- F3 IM3 strip robustness: fixed. Six form tests pass in my IM3 run
  (route.pii-scope.test.ts:168-226). The over-breadth limit (a capitalized
  `Word:` line is treated as a detail clause) is accepted in writing in
  evidence.md, "S3 Fix group". The prose-name form is caught by the
  known-details removal of the profile values.
- F4 MODEL_ID charset: fixed. `MODEL_ID` rejects key-shaped tokens
  (providers.ts:212) and roles.test.ts:266-287 asserts a bare key form gives
  `model: null` in the usage record. Passed in my run.
- F7 cache key: fixed. The cache key holds role and model only
  (providers.ts:477). The cached entry rechecks the key value
  (providers.ts:492-494). roles.test.ts:310-327 proves a rotated key yields a
  new provider. Passed in my run.
- F7 rate-limit raw error: fixed. Both catches log role and status JSON only
  (BM2 route.ts:101-105, IM3 route.ts:172-177). The marker tests pass in my
  runs (BM2 route.test.ts:202-240, IM3 route.pii-scope.test.ts:228-254).

## gates.sh key() edit (Green change)

The edit drops lines that start with `stdout | ` or `stderr | `. It hides no
real failure. I replicated the full key() pipeline over the recorded gate logs
(gates/s2/test-*.log against gates/s3/test-*.log): new keys are 0 for all four
workspaces. With the old filter, the only extra keys s2 to s3 are the two
`stdout |` framing headers of passing teacher tests (case 13 and case 15,
whose titles hold the word "error"). FAIL, AssertionError, and TS lines stay in
the key; I count 13 of those in gates/s3/test-bus-math-v2.log, which matches the
sanity claim in evidence.md. Console content lines under a framing header are
not dropped, only the header line itself.

