## Blocking finding

F1. The structured-output helper logs the served-model field of the response
body with no validation. `structured.ts:215` stores `result.model` into
`servedModel` when it is a string, and `structured.ts:245` passes
`servedModel ?? model` into `logAiRequest`, which `usage-log.ts:25` prints.
The chat path applies the finding (b) rule at both the read (providers.ts:312,
`safeModel`, with the key-form rejection in `MODEL_ID` at providers.ts:212) and
the log (providers.ts:336), and roles.test.ts:266 proves the
bare key form gives `model: null` there. The structured path bypasses that
rule. Test-strategy S3.7 states the phase rule: a usage record holds the served
model only under the finding (b) rule, and no log line holds a key. ADV-S3-8
names "the raw key in a log" as an attack to run against Green. A response body
that echoes a bare key form (the same condition the phase tests on the chat
path) reaches the console log unvalidated. Fix in Green: apply the same
bounded-model rule in structured.ts (reuse one validator, no second
implementation) and add a failing-first test in structured.test.ts that
mirrors roles.test.ts finding b.

## Nonblocking findings

- F2. `stripPersonDetails` removes each known account value everywhere with no
  minimum length (lesson-context.ts:89-92, split/join). BM2 passes
  `session.username` (route.ts:183) and `convex/auth.ts:117` accepts
  `username: v.string()` with no length floor. A one- or two-character username
  deletes every occurrence from the lesson math text. The accepted over-breadth
  limit in evidence.md covers capitalized labels only. No leak occurs.
- F3. The BM2 rate-limit catch binds no error and logs a fixed
  `status: null` (route.ts:101-105). The plan says log the status and the
  role. IM3 extracts the real status with `getErrorStatus`
  (IM3 route.ts:172-177). No leak occurs; the log cannot name the status.
- F4. The teacher ai-error-summary route still logs the raw error object in its
  outer catch (route.ts:137). The line predates S3 and the plan scoped finding
  (d) to the two chatbot routes. The structured helper never throws, so the
  error holds Convex and mapping text only. Fix it when the route is next
  touched.

